# Sathify code owners.
#
# GitHub reads this file to auto-request a review from whoever owns the files a
# pull request touches. On a project whose whole structure is "one module per
# person" (see CONTRIBUTING.md), that turns the ownership convention from a
# thing written in a README into a thing the tooling enforces.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE AND IS CURRENTLY INERT.
#
# Every rule below is commented out because the team's GitHub usernames are not
# known yet. To switch it on: replace @person-a .. @person-d with real
# usernames, uncomment the lines for the modules each person owns, and delete
# the rest. Nothing else in the repository depends on it, so a partly-filled
# file is fine — unmatched paths simply get no automatic reviewer.
#
# CODEOWNERS only *requests* reviews. It becomes a requirement only if you also
# turn on "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection; see the
# branch-protection section of CONTRIBUTING.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Shared code: everyone reviews ------------------------------------------
# These are the files four people edit at once, so they are the ones worth all
# four pairs of eyes. Keep this block enabled even if the per-module rules
# below are not.
#
# /backend/apps/core/               @person-a @person-b @person-c @person-d
# /backend/config/                  @person-a @person-b @person-c @person-d
# /backend/requirements/            @person-a @person-b @person-c @person-d
# /mobile/lib/core/                 @person-a @person-b @person-c @person-d
# /mobile/lib/shared/               @person-a @person-b @person-c @person-d
# /mobile/pubspec.yaml              @person-a @person-b @person-c @person-d
# /.github/                         @person-a @person-b @person-c @person-d

